{"id":"atonement-under-the-law","name":"Atonement, Under The Law","aliases":["Atonement"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:atonement-under-the-law"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Atonement","text":"This word does not occur in the Authorized Version of the New Testament except in Rom. 5:11, where in the Revised Version the word “reconciliation” is used. In the Old Testament it is of frequent occurrence. The meaning of the word is simply at-one-ment, i.e., the state of being at one or being reconciled, so that atonement is reconciliation. Thus it is used to denote the effect which flows from the death of Christ. But the word is also used to denote that by which this reconciliation is brought about, viz., the death of Christ itself; and when so used it means satisfaction, and in this sense to make an atonement for one is to make satisfaction for his offences (Ex. 32:30; Lev. 4:26; 5:16; Num. 6:11), and, as regards the person, to reconcile, to propitiate God in his behalf. By the atonement of Christ we generally mean his work by which he expiated our sins. But in Scripture usage the …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3722","lemma":"כָּפַר","xlit":"kâphar","gloss":"to cover","kjv":"appease, make, put off, reconcile","count":27,"share":0.44},{"strong":"H2403","lemma":"חַטָּאָה","xlit":"chaṭṭâʼâh","gloss":"an offence , and its penalty, occasion, sacrifice, or ex","kjv":"punishment, purifying, sin","count":21,"share":0.34},{"strong":"H2398","lemma":"חָטָא","xlit":"châṭâʼ","gloss":"to miss","kjv":"bear the blame, cleanse, commit, by fault","count":12,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H4196","lemma":"מִזְבֵּחַ","xlit":"mizbêach","gloss":"an altar","kjv":"altar","count":12,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H5930","lemma":"עֹלָה","xlit":"ʻôlâh","gloss":"a step or","kjv":"ascent, burnt offering, go up to. See also H5766","count":10,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H5545","lemma":"סָלַח","xlit":"çâlach","gloss":"to forgive","kjv":"forgive, pardon, spare","count":6,"share":0.1}]